From 0000000000000000000000000000000000000000 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Eric Reinsmidt <735251+ericreinsmidt@users.noreply.github.com>
Subject: [PATCH] The SD card's first start is at 3.3 V, the second at 1.8 V:
 plastron's U-Boot leaves the card at 3.3 V (no UHS in its sunxi driver),
 where TrimUI's boot loader left it at 1.8 V, so the 1.8 V first try (patch
 0007) failed on every boot, about 50 ms before the card was found. A card a
 restart left at 1.8 V is still found, one try later. Only the SD card's
 slot: the others start as before

---
--- a/drivers/mmc/host/sunxi-mmc.c
+++ b/drivers/mmc/host/sunxi-mmc.c
@@ -1411,14 +1411,19 @@
 
 	switch (ios->signal_voltage) {
 	case MMC_SIGNAL_VOLTAGE_330:
-		/* Until a card has answered, every other start is at 1.8 V. The
-		 * bootloader may have switched the card to 1.8 V to read it at
-		 * UHS speed, and it stays there until its power is cut, which a
-		 * rail shared with other parts never is; a fresh card starts at
-		 * 3.3 V. The core retries a start several times, so trying both
-		 * finds either. Once a card is there, requests are honoured. */
+		/* Until a card has answered, every other start is at 1.8 V. A
+		 * card left at 1.8 V for UHS speed stays there until its power
+		 * is cut, which a rail shared with other parts never is; a
+		 * fresh card starts at 3.3 V. The core retries a start several
+		 * times, so trying both finds either. Once a card is there,
+		 * requests are honoured. The SD card (sdc0) starts at 3.3 V
+		 * first: plastron's U-Boot leaves it there (no UHS in its sunxi
+		 * driver), and starting it at 1.8 V first cost every boot a
+		 * failed try, about 50 ms; 1.8 V comes second, for a restart
+		 * without a power cut. The other slots start at 1.8 V first, as
+		 * they did. */
 		if (!mmc->card && host->phy_index < ARRAY_SIZE(sunxi_mmc_start_tries) &&
-		    (sunxi_mmc_start_tries[host->phy_index]++ & 1) == 0) {
+		    (sunxi_mmc_start_tries[host->phy_index]++ & 1) == (host->phy_index == 0)) {
 			dev_info(mmc_dev(mmc), "starting the card at 1.8V\n");
 			sunxi_sel_pio_mode(host->pinctrl, MMC_SIGNAL_VOLTAGE_180);
 			return 0;
